as d[k] does"] [308 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [309 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [403 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [404 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [487 1 "// objectDir is object.__dir__: the instance's dictionary's keys and its class's attributes."] [531 1 "// superArgs are super()'s zero arguments: the running function's first argument and its __class__ cell."] [588 2 "// method_reduce (classobject.c): getattr(self, the function's name)"] [603 2 "// functions as descriptors, bound methods"] [610 2 "// types.MethodType(func, instance) (method_new)"] [670 2 "// slot wrappers"] [698 2 "// classmethod, staticmethod"] [716 3 "// a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor: a builtin_function_or_method bound to the class (dict.fromkeys)"] [812 2 "// property"] [944 2 "// __slots__' members"] [1000 2 "// super"] [1047 5 "// a built-in type's method, or a method descriptor in a heap type's dict (methodDescrs: _ast's AST,"] [1048 5 "// queue 202c: super().__init__ in a node class's subclass)"] [1095 2 "// mappingproxy"] [1097 2 "// mappingproxy(mapping), over a dict (PY6a: enum's __members__); other mappings are the data model's"] [1111 2 "// a built-in type's own slots' wrappers (ownSlots, registry.go) are in its __dict__ too (PY5e, part 2b)"] [1119 14 "// a built-in type's attribute descriptors (type.__dict__['__annotations__']: annotationlib)"] [1138 2 "// mappingproxy_richcompare: the mapping's own comparison (queue 202: mappingproxy({}) == {} was False; test_re's"] [1139 2 "// test_getattr compares a pattern's groupindex with a dict)"] [1162 2 "// the mapping's own views (mappingproxy_keys: a set-like dict_keys; queue 225: typing's tests take vars(C).keys() | ...)"] [1357 3 "// recursive_issubclass's check_class"] [1544 2 "// __module__ is func.go's (PY6d's R5: the function's module), which this init's order let override this one"] [1547 1 "// excSlots are the __slots__ values of exceptions (an exception class's instances are *Exception, not"] [1548 1 "// *Instance): PY6a, by the integration's owner, for test_exceptions' slotted exception classes."] [1551 1 "// setTypeBases is type.__bases__'s setter (typeobject.c's type_set_bases; PY6b's request: typing.NamedTuple"] [1552 1 "// assigns a class's bases): a heap type's bases replaced by types of the same instance layout, its MRO and its"] [1553 1 "// subclasses' computed again and their slots refilled."] [1615 14 "// the type attribute cache: an MRO set"] [1624 1 "// newStaticBase is tp_new_wrapper's staticbase (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_bad_new): t, or"] [1625 1 "// the first base along __base__ whose __new__ is not a Python class's own (slot_tp_new)."] [1633 1 "// newOrigin is the built-in type whose __new__ t's tp_new is (inherited along __base__ from the first one"] [1634 1 "// that defines it), CPython's tp_new pointer compared."] [1648 1 "// newAliases: the built-in types whose own __new__ here is CPython's inherited one (defaultdict's is dict_new)"] [1651 1 "// isNewWrapper: v is a built-in type's __new__ (tp_new_wrapper); a class whose __new__ is one keeps the"] [1652 1 "// __new__ it inherits (update_one_slot's special case), so that class C(list): __new__ = object.__new__"] [1653 1 "// makes lists"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[122 29] [140 37] [177 37] [190 67] [201 63] [206 68] [211 67] [227 37] [244 37] [266 37] [302 37] [306 25] [320 38] [325 37] [335 37] [382 38] [387 37] [405 26] [419 29] [446 25] [448 38] [466 37] [490 25] [492 24] [507 24] [563 26] [573 23] [628 34] [631 36] [639 54] [662 55] [701 49] [717 32] [724 50] [778 21] [779 36] [790 43] [843 38] [851 28] [853 56] [893 42] [919 50] [929 53] [934 48] [935 26] [950 31] [951 32] [960 30] [967 31] [1003 43] [1042 51] [1049 29] [1055 36] [1083 21] [1089 21] [1102 38] [1117 23] [1118 36] [1130 25] [1152 76] [1191 71] [1230 39]